WEBVTT

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:05.690
Now, come. I'll play with you.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.110
Nox Nyctores Gigant,

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.200
Take-Mikazuchi!

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.130
Nulliplex restriction mechanism release.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:36.180
Dimensional interruption imaginary number developing.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.900
Connecting to congenital border.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.030
Activating Tsukuyomi Unit.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.000
It's futile.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:17.640
Not even you can pierce Tsukuyomi's absolute defense.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:46.660
Four years will pass before you can fire again.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.130
Until then, sleep, young one.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:34.020
Rebel 3: The Observing Eye

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.150
Huh? Wh-What is that?
Rebel 3: The Observing Eye

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.150
Rebel 3: The Observing Eye

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:41.820
Noel Vermillion!

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.120
Mr. Hazama?

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:54.330
<i>Observe</i> me, Noel Vermillion!

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.930
That counts! That totally counts!

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.390
You psychopath!

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:17.360
Long time no see.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.780
Rags, my boy!

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:26.870
Terumi!

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:32.750
Cease this.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:35.750
Now that events have changed,

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.590
you don't even have a ghost of a chance of winning.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:39.960
Like I give a shit!

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.550
Ouroboros!

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:02.280
Huh? What?

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.030
You...

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:06.860
Mr. Ragna!

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.490
You suck!

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:12.700
You've always sucked, and always will, Rags!

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.540
Bastard...

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:21.920
Ah, I'm done.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:26.260
Hold it right there, Terumi...

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:27.430
That was...

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:30.390
You ended up <i>observing</i> him, didn't you, Noel?

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:31.470
What?

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:38.060
Your Eye fell upon that man and recognized his existence.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:40.400
Ended up observing him?

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:53.700
Wow!

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:55.750
That frightened me!

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.330
That earthquake sure was something, wasn't it, Dr. Litchi?

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.290
Agreed. I wonder what caused it.

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:05.340
I'm going to go take a look outside.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.510
Linhua!

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.520
That smoke...

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:17.430
Is it related to the shaking?

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:28.490
Is this the place, Sis?

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:40.580
Huh? We're back here?

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:46.510
Kokonoe, that man has returned.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:50.300
Yeah, I was watching.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:53.220
Wh-Who's there?

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.220
You're letting 'em listen in?

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:00.270
Whatever. I don't care.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:05.230
I waited a long-ass time for this.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:10.570
I'm gonna erase him from this world like the mistake he is!

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:14.530
Reign in your temper. It is disgraceful.

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.240
Disgraceful's fine by me!

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:20.910
You certainly got beat to a pulp.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.500
This place should be suitable for you to recuperate.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:30.050
A plethora of tasks await to be done.

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:32.630
For me as well as you two.

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:37.850
The world turns.

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:39.680
Everything goes round and round.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:44.400
The never-changing conclusion has crumbled and we have welcomed a new dawn.

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:46.690
However...

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:54.530
Uh, um, who was that girl?

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:58.330
She just teleported in and out! And also that time with Mr. Hazama!

00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.540
Why'd you call him "Terumi"?

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.330
A-A-And...

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:05.500
You...

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:06.590
Why...

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:09.090
Why do I feel that you're...

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:13.340
...close to me in some way?

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:19.180
I don't have any memories of when I was little, or rather...

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:20.680
They're really unclear.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:24.520
Could it be that you know something?

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:27.730
Doesn't ring a bell.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:31.780
Now buzz off. Go mind your own business.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:36.240
Y-You don't have to say it like that...

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.290
If that's what you want!

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:58.390
Come on out.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:03.350
You managed to sense us.

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:05.890
You're leaking bloodthirst like a broken faucet.

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:07.810
Couldn't ignore it even if I wanted to.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:09.820
Say, bounty hunter,

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.280
is that a Nox Nyctores with you?

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:14.280
How very perceptive of you.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:17.700
You're well deserving of your reputation, Ragna the Bloodedge.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:18.910
Well, then.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:19.910
Shit.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:22.490
I'll be taking the Azure Grimoire!

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:25.500
Not you too!

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:50.940
Splendid!

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.120
That hit the spot.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.450
The mind meld is going well too.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:08.960
She ain't the Azure Successor for nothing.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.340
Hazama of the Intelligence Department speaking here.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:16.720
Would you be so kind as to transfer me to Relius Clover from Engineering?

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:20.550
Speaking.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:24.180
Hi, old buddy. How's it going?

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:25.600
Oh, Terumi.

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:27.980
It went well, I gather.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.850
Why, yes, it did.

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.360
Oh, that's right.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:37.440
The Azure was inherited by Prime Field No. 12.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:40.360
Oh? No.12, is it?

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:43.120
I was certain she was a failure.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:47.660
Not at all! I was surprised how solid she was, myself.

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:51.120
She goes by Noel Vermillion, but...

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:55.300
Oh? Guess you don't really care about this kinda stuff.

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.590
Well, can't blame ya.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:10:59.050
Let's see...

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:00.800
Well, how about this?

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:04.010
The Monolith's been setup without a hitch.

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:07.600
We're looking at another two, three days until the cocoon forms.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:13.770
And that leaves us only with our lil' Noel left.

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.980
We just need to get our paws on the Azure successor

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:18.400
and then preparations for the God Killer will be A-okay!

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:21.740
How do you plan to awaken the Murakumo Unit within her?

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:26.240
Just gonna flip the switch on her limiter, the Nox Nyctores Bolverk.

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:28.250
How dull.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:30.910
So you'd already guessed?

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:36.920
In any case, I'd like to see No.12 for myself.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:38.960
I will make way for Kagutsuchi.

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:41.930
Well ain't that a treat?

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:45.100
I gotta say though, given the whole "I hate everything" shtick,

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:49.520
I had my money on No.13 becoming the successor.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:51.850
Guess we were both wrong!

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:56.650
It was 12, the overlooked piece of junk, who ended up winning the big prize!

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:02.490
As a researcher, I bet you can't wait to see it.

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:04.990
Where are you getting at?

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:06.870
Nowhere at all.

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:10.200
All right, I'll see you at Iwasu first thing, 'kay?

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:11.960
We can discuss the nitty-gritty details there.

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:18.170
Oh boy. Things are getting so <i>interesting</i>!

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:22.050
In order to awaken the Murakumo Unit within Noel Vermillion,

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:24.760
I'm gonna need a helluva lot of hatred.

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:29.060
Enough to swallow up the world, give or take a bit.

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:34.100
And to that end, I'll make good use of them.

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:38.020
Those precious friends of hers.

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:43.990
Hazama of the Intelligence Department speaking.

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:46.200
May I inquire on the condition of Major Jin Kisaragi?

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:49.160
I understand.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.950
By all means, keep on looking after him.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:53.870
Oh, and before I forget.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:56.670
Would you let First Lieutenant Tsubaki Yayoi of the Zero Squadron know

00:12:56.670 --> 00:13:00.250
that her presence is required at the 3rd Hiearchical City of Iwasu?

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:50.050
Yeah, you're right, Sis. He doesn't seem to be at the top of his game.

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:54.430
I'm glad you found him before any of the other bounty hunters did, Sis.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:55.680
Balls!

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:01.110
And now, the Azure will be ours!

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:06.950
You can't get me like that.

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:12.740
You're not getting away!

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:13.620
Sis!

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:17.120
Where are you aiming at?

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:24.090
Ragna the Bloodedge...

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.590
Him...

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:08.720
Meow?

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:11.590
Whoopsie!

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:14.100
Mew hurt, Good Guy?

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:16.890
This isn't even the best spot for a catnap.

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:19.310
You know this man?

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:20.350
Meowbe?

00:15:21.390 --> 00:15:23.150
I was pawsitive I'd smelled Good Guy around.

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:24.900
So I came to have a little look-see!

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:25.770
I see.

00:15:26.270 --> 00:15:28.280
He seems to be badly injured.

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:31.030
You should take him to a doctor.

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:33.780
A ducktor?

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.990
Dawctor...

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:39.080
That's the Boobie Lady!

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:18.620
Jin! Saya!

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:20.950
What happened?! What in the...

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.510
J-Jin...

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:36.850
Jin...

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:40.600
S-Saya...

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:57.120
Hey kid, need a hand?

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:01.750
Well shit, Rags. That looks kinda painful!

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:04.580
So? How much does it hurt on a scale of 1 to 10?

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:06.750
Whoops, don't have enough fingers to count that high!

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:09.380
Bastard...

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:13.300
Hey now, no need to get up in arms!

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:15.840
Still, you're stronger than I thought.

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:18.850
Way stronger than that nun I just wasted.

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:23.270
Poor thing, blubbering for her life!

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:26.940
Stop lying, you piece of shit...

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:31.520
Jin, take Saya and run...

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:33.320
Jin!

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:34.940
Brother.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:37.450
This is your fault, Brother.

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:42.330
I'm taking the long-haired twerp with me.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:45.410
W-Wait...

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:49.830
The name's Terumi. Yuuki Terumi.

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:54.130
Be sure to write, if you survive that is. Got it, Rags?

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:00.510
So long, Brother.

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:10.020
Where am I?

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:11.520
Whoa!

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:12.860
He opened his eyes!

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:13.900
He opened them!

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:14.980
He did!

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:19.820
Now you're down to 8 lives, Good Guy!

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:21.530
Tao...

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:23.700
Tao, I have to continue his treatment.

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:26.120
Could you ask everyone to leave?

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:27.500
I'm on it meow!

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:30.420
All right lil' ones, follow the Tao!

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:32.040
Yay!

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:38.590
These wounds come from a Nox Nyctores, don't they?

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:40.970
And who the hell are you?

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:45.180
A doctor. From Orient Town.

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.190
Why won't you draw on my soul?

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:55.980
You could use your abilities if you did, right?

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:00.110
The Azure Grimoire...

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:07.250
Humeowngous titties! Boobie Lady!

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:08.620
"Boobie Lady"?

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:09.250
Humeowngous titties...

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:10.210
Is that what you go by?

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:14.130
N-No! It's Litchi! Litchi Faye-Ling!

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:17.130
Stop that, Tao! I mean it!

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:19.670
Good Guy's all remewed now!

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:22.050
Less napping, more playing with me!

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:23.090
Ow!

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:25.810
Get off me! Scram!

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:29.180
That's enough, Tao! He's not fully healed yet!

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:30.890
He needs to rest.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:32.150
I meow...

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:35.570
I'll watch over Good Guy like a guard cat!

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:36.360
Huh?

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:41.860
Watch over Good Guy, make him better, and then we can go play!

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:43.160
Play, play, play!

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:44.160
I swear...
Play, play, play!

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:45.030
Play, play, play!

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:49.120
What the heck?! Why'd he have to be all mean about it?!

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:52.460
He may be rebel, but he <i>did</i> save me...

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:56.460
I thought maybe he had his reasons, but he played me for a fool!

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:03.430
Seriously, why is it that I can't stop thinking about him?

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:09.810
Snap out of it, Second Lieutenant Noel Vermillion!

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:11.730
It's all in your head!

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:21.030
All right!

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:25.570
First Lieutenant Tsubaki Yayoi, reporting for duty, sir.

00:22:26.110 --> 00:22:29.200
My apologies for having you come all this way.

00:22:29.200 --> 00:22:30.240
Not at all, sir.

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:35.370
Well, First Lieutenant, there's a certain sensitive matter I'd like you to take care of.

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:40.170
These orders actually come straight from Joint Command.

00:22:41.130 --> 00:22:44.420
I'm to brief you on this mission myself, verbally.

00:22:44.420 --> 00:22:45.130
Yes, sir!

00:22:46.340 --> 00:22:48.050
First Lieutenant Tsubaki Yayoi, you are tasked

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:53.300
to seek out Major Jin Kisaragi and Second Lieutenant Noel Vermillion...

00:22:53.680 --> 00:22:55.970
...and eliminate them.

00:22:55.970 --> 00:22:56.770
What?

00:23:01.730 --> 00:23:04.980
Even with this and that, you're still doing well, Ragna.

00:23:05.440 --> 00:23:05.940
Episode 4,
"Master This-and-That Appears".

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:08.740
Rebel 4: Probalistic Events

00:23:08.740 --> 00:23:10.990
That's not even the right title!
